ng i  mean  do you think they will be willing to  look at this is this a sort of change  they'd be happy to make  uh not happy to make perhaps but  it will be something they have to make i  think  because it used to be that  the elite songwriters of course could  always make a living out of songwriting  but there was a layer underneath as well  um and and they could make a living  during um  in the physical era and  they um could manage to  push themselves up to the upper level  uh through having you know the time  and being able to afford to spend time  on becoming better songwriters  and uh it's you know it's a talent  but it's also a craft and you have to  hone your craft  with that in mind i mean just how real  is the possibility then if it's  if it's just not paying enough money  under the the way the current system  works well we're  we're gonna miss out we're gonna miss  out on some real talent aren't we  i'm afraid so uh i mean i'm uh  i'm an example of what i  mean because before we won the  eurovision song contest with waterloo  benny anderson and i have been had been  in a rat race we were running around  producing  other people's records writing songs for  other people even going on  tours you know in different  constellations just to pay the rent  but from waterloo when the royalties  came  pouring in from that time we could  afford to say no to  everything else and just concentrate on  the writing  and that's when you get better at it and  that's what i wish for more songwriters  today  for in terms of the public in terms of  us as listeners to music  um do we pay enough then should we be  expecting to pay more  for streaming services because it is  cheap at the moment  it is very cheap and and this is a  legacy from the  beginning of of streaming when it  actually  saved the music industry from illegal  downloading  uh but it's time i think and i i  i i think that the the streaming  services  are thinking about um higher prices in  the future  because after all to get all the music  from  from the whole world from every century  for 9.99 is is you know very cheap  um i can't let you go without asking  about abba directly um because  people wouldn't forgive me my father  wouldn't forgive me  joe our cameraman who's a superfan would  not forgive me  um you have written music  which all these decades later  has stood the test of time that there  isn't much in the world of pop which  you can listen to in 2021 that still  sounds as fresh as  as the day it was released how on earth  did you manage that  yeah i you know it's it  i'm constantly amazed at that  and and really i don't know how it  happened  we we just recorded you know the songs  the best we could
 

